codex
Implemented a verified Track A generator based on the paper’s Theorem 10 NAE-3-SAT reduction. The paper confirms NP-completeness for fixed \(k=\ell=2\) and identifies the excluded polynomial regimes in Theorems 2–4 and 9. [Paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1806.03426)

Key results:

- Shipping preset: 174 variables, 348 clauses.
- All G1–G9 gated checks pass.
- Random guessing: 0/200,000.
- Five adversarial attacks: each 0/8 successes.
- DPLL baseline: 4,001 nodes and 4,261,268 clause inspections, unsolved.
- Bare oracle loop: hardened, 0/3 solved.
- Worst-case answer: 763 characters, approximately 191 tokens, 174 atoms.
- Hinted/placebo diagnostics were attempted but OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 quota errors; the harness-produced error records are preserved and reported honestly.

Deliverables:

- [gen_1806_03426.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1806.03426/gen_1806_03426.py:26)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1806.03426/selftest_report.json:1)
