codex
Implemented and verified the Track A generator using the paper’s Theorem 10 reduction from balanced regular NAE-3-SAT.

Key results:

- Shipping preset: `n=174`, degree 6, 348 clauses.
- G1–G9 pass.
- Random guessing: 0/200,000.
- Five adversarial attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- DPLL baseline: 4,001 nodes and 4,261,268 clause inspections without solving.
- Bare oracle loop: 0/3 solved; all responses parsed and failed exact verification.
- G9 hinted/placebo runs were attempted, but OpenRouter returned key-limit errors, recorded without counting them as failures.

Deliverables:

- [Generator module](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1806.03426/gen_1806_03426.py:26)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1806.03426/selftest_report.json)
- [Bare oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1806.03426/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Structural-hint transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1806.03426/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo-hint transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1806.03426/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)
- [README and audit narrative](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1806.03426/README.md)

The final audit re-scored every saved oracle reply with the current verifier, matched the README demo exactly against `render()`, and passed compilation and interface checks.
