Rejected honestly; no generator ships.

Theorem 10 proves worst-case NP-completeness for \(k=\ell=2\), but not hardness of the generated planted distribution. A proper break-count WalkSAT attack solved:

- Shipping preset: 8/8, median ≈0.016 seconds
- Medium preset: 8/8
- Hard preset: 8/8

The corrected self-test therefore fails G5 and G6. Track B does not rescue the family because there is no compact answer-finding route distinct from the mechanical search. See the [full paper](https://arxiv.org/html/1806.03426v1).

